<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:23:09Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>🔴 Surgery on Pope Leo's cancerous lung nodule went well, Vatican says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:797d3a88dd472f2a7e7696a9cf6f7437659d48eb86503dc43856275c767b1473</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:44:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week--42462f7a7f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c2260fae17387a112443a6e1ca2777e0927da3778486d149069b54854b0fa54</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:33:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing--2d8cf39e1327.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing" /><summary type="html">Duane Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump asks Greece ambassador to resign amid ethics scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d20fea6d0d391a8b6cfd1ad04235e8fa1de2087407dfc133a750c61c919a1b</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal--24c18b5f16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's administration has asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign, the White House said Tuesday, amid allegations that she sought money from a Trump supporter and accepted lavish hospitality from wealthy Greek businessmen. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kabila launches new coalition with M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daaeee50071f995a31f907a93a7140f4ead0fc45e7dd118092439c39268b4cc8</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:21:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23--ed60166777a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Joseph Kabila has been named leader of a new rebel coalition, vowing to topple the government. Also, Africa's largest ever IPO has been extended. And Formula ⁠1 ⁠will return to ⁠Africa in ​the early 2030s, once a new circuit is built in Rwanda.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>French MPs pass sweeping bill to combat sexual and gender-based violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d32ee6a43903ea3a1a51346cf89afd23a0b9d66089336d249a7795f88aaebfb</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:03:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-mps-pass-sweeping-bill-to-combat-sexual-and-gender-based-violence--5235867145cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-mps-pass-sweeping-bill-to-combat-sexual-and-gender-based-violence" /><summary type="html">The National Assembly overwhelmingly passed the so-called “comprehensive” bill against sexist and sexual violence on Tuesday. The focus now shifts to the more conservative Senate, with the bill’s supporters fearing that its main advances could be watered down, even though the government insists it will act as guarantor of the bill’s ambition. Sponsored in the Assembly by eight political groups, from the Communists to Les Républicains (LR), the text was adopted by 503 votes to 0. Only the LFI (La France Insoumise) deputies abstained, denouncing in particular the removal of measures aimed at protecting foreign women. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to 40 years to life for Tupac Shakur murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa305d8f030ed53db827d79f7626e6685e609a25e458797878c78c8c38e03219</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:57:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder--2d6357adbe6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane “Keffe D” Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France's youth undergoing 'a crisis of hope'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25964c11e88abe5fff85da1dfe87715d40c2d6a76060f0e6db618527e9432e06</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:33:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-youth-undergoing-a-crisis-of-hope--deece93fa1c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-youth-undergoing-a-crisis-of-hope" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people joined rallies across France on Tuesday to support protesting high school students, boosting a movement that poses a major challenge to President Emmanuel Macron as his term in office winds down. Some 161,500 people turned out, according to the interior ministry -- more than double the 71,500 it gave for the last nationwide demonstrations on Thursday last week. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Andrew Smith, Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary's London, says that France's youth is undergoing "a crisis of hope" which is pushing "the anger and the sense that something has to change".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e432308b71dea07a575317a1944af565d282dc719286e246a792372154e7bada</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:06:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit--84d6778d9333.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands rally across France as high school protests gather strength</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f879d82ac35ef7f89cdf2a4adf9a0c15d5a1ab05aae4f0ddd30b74d86c90e1e1</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:21:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261013-tens-of-thousands-rally-across-france-as-high-school-protests-gather-strength--7c387a32d594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261013-tens-of-thousands-rally-across-france-as-high-school-protests-gather-strength" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people rallied across France on Tuesday in support of protesting high school students, with unions putting turnout at 480,000, as anger over school conditions and alleged police violence fuels a growing movement challenging President Emmanuel Macron’s government ahead of planned cost-of-living demonstrations on Saturday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France's fed-up youth: Can presidential candidates connect with student movement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498a4e7f53bf6ce7182105bb27e8825fe1e69edaaea8cb93a86b8f2134a3c967</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:10:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261013-france-s-fed-up-youth-can-presidential-candidates-connect-with-student-movement--803e75a12ac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261013-france-s-fed-up-youth-can-presidential-candidates-connect-with-student-movement" /><summary type="html">Will it be autumn recess to the rescue for a beleaguered French government? Ministers no doubt counting the days until Friday evening when the holidays start in hopes that an unexpected student movement disappears as quickly as it materialized. A movement sparked three weeks ago by deteriorating conditions in a Paris area high school may take a leave of absence… but what about demands for a generation that feels left behind by cost cutting? Only one party’s sided vocally with the students since the very start, Jean-Luc Mélenchon’s far-left France Unbowed.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>ISS amid global conflict: A rare bastion of 'scientific collaboration' between the East and West</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f33f0fd28e49de3e366ce76c9b6068cd936b0a1fb64bfd9d48fd8a20cc1d8ff</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:22:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:53:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-iss-amid-global-conflict-a-rare-bastion-of-scientific-collaboration-between-the-east-and-we--01170922784a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-iss-amid-global-conflict-a-rare-bastion-of-scientific-collaboration-between-the-east-and-west" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Alban Guyomarc'h, Researcher in Space Geopolitics at Paris's École Normale Supérieure School of Higher Learning. As a new era of space rivalry unfolds, the International Space Station remains one of the last bastions of cooperation between geopolitical adversaries. For Guyomarc'h, the latest ISS mission is more than a remarkable technological achievement. "It's one of the rare collaboration spaces we still have today in a very conflictual era".</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Digital distrust and polarisation: 'We need to get back to engaging with one another as a society'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af269b75915f3b9defd817a7a838433a31a5f0387982d931c03d6068337b0463</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:23:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:39:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-digital-distrust-and-polarisation-we-need-to-get-back-to-engaging-with-one-another-as-a-soc--34372d50a6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-digital-distrust-and-polarisation-we-need-to-get-back-to-engaging-with-one-another-as-a-society" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Valdemar Osted, partner and head of technology at Danish digital consultancy Common Consultancy. Can the fear of disinformation become as dangerous to democracy as disinformation itself? Osted challenges widely circulated claims that attacks on Russian data centres have triggered a sudden collapse in online engagement among supporters of Donald Trump and Germany's far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD). Drawing on social media monitoring and research into inauthentic behaviour, Osted reports finding no unusual decline in Facebook interactions following the attacks.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: Israeli army accused of arbitrary arrests and detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8910dcfe91bffb17df4500a7e767434ab05429527ed81ea65a7375cb9e4504b</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:23:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:28:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261013-syria-israeli-army-accused-arbitrary-arrests-detention--ad59aa39dde2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261013-syria-israeli-army-accused-arbitrary-arrests-detention" /><summary type="html">The Israeli army has arrested more than 200 people in southern Syria since the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s regime in December 2024, according to the Sijil Centre, which tracks Israeli activity in Syria. The Israeli military says it is targeting “suspected terrorists”. Witnesses, for their part, have denounced the arbitrary arrests, while former detainees and their loved ones have raised serious concerns over conditions in detention.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Student protesters tell police to join them in Paris demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfa1ae7c386223b1d0ffae35a0c54451c3e5a9f3ee29af948688969aecd2391d</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:23:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:04:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-student-protesters-tell-police-to-join-them-in-paris-demonstrations--c37f571fa6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-student-protesters-tell-police-to-join-them-in-paris-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">As student-led protests in Paris came to a close on Tuesday, demonstrators chanted "join us, join us" to police officers, who took off their helmets to cheers of the crowd. "When police take off their helmets, it's a sign that things are getting calmer," said FRANCE 24 reporter Claire Paccalin. Broader demonstrations are set to take place across France on Saturday over the cost of living, as well as further student protests, with the two potentially merging into a substantial movement. "But many of the young people I have spoken to today say they will not participate on Saturday," Paccalin said.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: French students ‘not giving up the fight’ as 480,000 join new day of school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9651669e2a19f3f532911947e0199e56e92b4f6094c180aca2742ad2de7bcbf5</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T16:16:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions--ed166873d347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions" /></entry><entry><title>France: Student anger rages as tear gas and fires hit Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09cbc41062cc5ae309cd285237c1f52394cdde087c16c0f2ec574e3da622c8ff</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T16:03:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-student-anger-rages-as-tear-gas-and-fires-hit-paris--558c8f11c3c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-student-anger-rages-as-tear-gas-and-fires-hit-paris" /><summary type="html">Around 480,000 people took part in nationwide student demonstrations across France on Tuesday, according to student and school unions, up from the previous week’s mobilisation. In Paris, the demonstration ended with tear gas and fires, as tensions escalated. Claire Paccalin has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>From Paris to Marseille, high school protests continue across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db2baae7eb43cf0ba02690f814fe29c7b4bec935e4175127653a753cbf23271</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:40:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-from-paris-to-marseille-high-school-protests-continue-across-france--a79550cc049c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-from-paris-to-marseille-high-school-protests-continue-across-france" /><summary type="html">Student protests continue across France, with marches taking place in cities including Lille and Marseille while pupils in Paris stage fresh school blockades using wheelie bins. Demonstrators are calling for better learning conditions, saying government measures announced so far have failed to address their concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Kenya, recycled plastic gets a second life as chess pieces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7778e0878a20d4c700aa33033bd6fc12ca9ed333ad4e0914f82e61ef3951e3b</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:28:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces--70350efdf983.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces" /><summary type="html">In Nairobi, a project is helping children develop focus, patience and critical thinking through chess, using pieces made from recycled plastic waste.</summary></entry><entry><title>Broken children: France confronts crisis of sexual violence against minors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e98f488463926b3b97d80c4bb58ccf1b6d86ae55ff571f2f4f66d158f56be9e4</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261013-broken-children-france-confronts-crisis-of-sexual-violence-against-minors--cc7f845b26eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261013-broken-children-france-confronts-crisis-of-sexual-violence-against-minors" /><summary type="html">In France, a new "comprehensive law" aims to strengthen preventative measures, the judicial process and support for child victims of sexual violence. Yet advocacy groups, lawyers, and healthcare professionals point out that the legislation has numerous shortcomings. We take a closer look in this edition of France in Focus. Warning: viewers may find parts of this report disturbing.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>French youth demand answers as education protests enter third week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9a5d257ac5ab09bfaa9120a93aacf4a8c93a5c452ae47592691948709887edd</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-youth-demand-answers-as-education-protests-enter-third-week--b581967edb3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-youth-demand-answers-as-education-protests-enter-third-week" /><summary type="html">French students have continued nationwide protests for a third week, demanding more funding for education, better teaching conditions and more staff. The government’s plan to recruit 3,000 substitute teachers has failed to satisfy demonstrators, who are calling for an additional €10 billion in education spending. Backed by teachers and unions, protesters warn the mobilisation will continue as the government prepares budget cuts.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Felipe VI says Ceuta is ‘inalienable’ part of Spain in landmark visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:937470b8e46c40c11b879731205ec7d69ec66a736ccf118e787a727214f27978</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx--f9df8bcf336a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta on Tuesday for the first time in 14 years, with the monarch reaffirming Spain’s sovereignty over the North African enclaves claimed by Morocco. The landmark visit comes amid strained relations with Rabat and the aftermath of a mass migrant influx that saw makeshift camps cleared ahead of the royals’ arrival.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications amid renewed anti-immigrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a05e3f08778024ced79e1a7c4a42723d7c912a96ad06fc0dd397e4b12e2ccda</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:15:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests--0599fa64feef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests" /><summary type="html">Tensions have flared in South Africa after a court ruling prompted the government to open its application system to all foreign nationals, regardless of their legal status. Despite applications remaining subject to approval, anti-immigrant protests erupted outside several Home Affairs offices, forcing authorities to temporarily suspend refugee and asylum applications. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian forces enter key Tigray town, raising fears among residents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bbb578eeeb9c8bd724212c3b57b7f4290e6937a1b95fea0fbb19949da06ca8c</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:13:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents--da75969b90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces and their allies have entered a key town in northern Tigray near the Eritrean border after rebel fighters withdrew. As the conflict intensifies, residents fear further violence and instability. Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:836e30e51020d28e51e3f1835e406c95c92d2cf00eb5a8fe02c1cc40a159cf27</id><updated>2026-10-13T21:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T14:59:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency--752369db782e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency" /><summary type="html">Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.</summary></entry></feed>
